---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Install — LemmaScript"
  description="Two ways to install LemmaScript: the npm package plus the agent skills, or the source kit with everything bundled."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">// install</span>
      <h1>Two ways <em>in</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Install the package and add the agent skills — or clone the source kit with
        everything bundled. Use the package if you're <b>using</b> LemmaScript; take the
        kit if you're <b>changing</b> it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- OPTION A: THE PACKAGE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// option a</span>
        <h2>The package.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          The standard setup: the <code class="inline">lsc</code> toolchain from npm, plus
          the skills that teach your agent to drive it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="step-n">1</span><h3>Check the prerequisites</h3></div>
          <p>Node ≥ 18, Dafny ≥ 4.x (the engine that does the checking), and git.</p>
          <div class="codeblock">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">terminal</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-anno">$</span> node -v          <span class="t-cmt"># ≥ 18</span>
<span class="t-anno">$</span> dafny --version  <span class="t-cmt"># ≥ 4.x</span></pre>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="step-n">2</span><h3>Install the package</h3></div>
          <p>One global install puts <code class="inline">lsc</code> — and companions like <code class="inline">lsc claimcheck</code> — on your PATH.</p>
          <div class="codeblock">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">terminal</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-anno">$</span> npm install -g lemmascript</pre>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="step-n">3</span><h3>Add the skills</h3></div>
          <p>Mount the skills repo at your project's skills directory. Your agent picks them up and drives the whole loop itself — contracts, checks, iteration.</p>
          <div class="codeblock">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">terminal</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-anno">$</span> git submodule add https://github.com/midspiral/lemmascript-skills .claude/skills</pre>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="step-n">4</span><h3>Check something</h3></div>
          <p>Point it at a file — or at your whole project — and watch the contracts hold.</p>
          <div class="codeblock">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">terminal</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-anno">$</span> lsc check --backend=dafny src/

<span class="t-kw">✓</span> charge   correct
<span class="t-cmt">1 / 1 correct · 0.4s</span></pre>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OPTION B: FROM SOURCE -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// option b</span>
        <h2>From source: <code class="inline-h2">lemmascript-kit</code></h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Working on the toolchain itself, or want the tools and skills pinned together?
          The kit bundles the toolchain source and the skills as git submodules — one
          clone, one setup script, skills already in place.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="step-n">1</span><h3>Clone the kit</h3></div>
          <p>It uses submodules, so clone recursively, then bootstrap.</p>
          <div class="codeblock">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">terminal</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-anno">$</span> git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/midspiral/lemmascript-kit.git
<span class="t-anno">$</span> cd lemmascript-kit
<span class="t-anno">$</span> ./setup.sh</pre>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="step">
          <div class="step-head"><span class="step-n">2</span><h3>Run from source</h3></div>
          <p>The same commands, straight out of the source tree. The skills write the CLI as <code class="inline">npx lsc</code> — in the kit, substitute this form (or <code class="inline">npm link</code> the package).</p>
          <div class="codeblock">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">terminal</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-anno">$</span> npx tsx LemmaScript/tools/src/lsc.ts check --backend=dafny path/to/file.ts</pre>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout callout-info kit-note">
        <span class="mark">i</span>
        <div>
          <b>Skills included.</b> The kit already mounts the skills at
          <code class="inline">.claude/skills/</code> — no separate step. Updating either
          piece is normal git discipline: bump the submodule, review the diff.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NEXT -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="closing">
        <p>
          From here: the full reference, the contract language, and everything that snaps
          onto the core.
        </p>
        <div class="head-actions">
          <a href="https://docs.lemmascript.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Read the docs →</a>
          <a href="/ecosystem" class="btn btn-secondary">Explore the ecosystem</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .steps { list-style: none; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-12); max-width: 760px; }
  .step-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-3); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .step-n { width: 28px; height: 28px; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: var(--r-full); display: grid; place-items: center;
    background: var(--state-verified-bg); border: 1px solid var(--accent-dim); color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-small); font-weight: 600; }
  .step-head h3 { font-size: var(--fs-h3); }
  .step > p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--fs-small); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); max-width: 60ch; }

  .inline-h2 { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.95em; }
  .lede b { color: var(--text-primary); }

  .kit-note { margin-top: var(--sp-8); max-width: 760px; }

  .closing { max-width: 68ch; }
  .closing p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--sp-6); }
  .head-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--sp-3); flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
